@div segment A

@div sa-gida A

$ (unknown. no. lines missing)
A.A.1. [...] X A₂ X X [...]
?#tr.en: …… in battle and fight …….
?#tr.en: You gave …… to your offspring (?) …….
?#tr.en: …… shepherd @wRN{Šulgi}, you spread fearsomeness over the foreign countries.
?#tr.en: …… shepherd, your offspring (?) will praise you duly.
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.1

A.A.2. [...] X me₃-a šen X [...]
#lem: X; X; me[battle]; šen[battle]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.2

A.A.3. [...] X UŠ URUGAL GUR₅ a-zu X [...] X mu-na-a-šum₂
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; azu[doctor]; X; X; X; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.3

A.A.4. [...]-ta# sipad šul-gi ni₂ kur₂-ra i₃-ru
#lem: X; sipad[shepherd]; Šulgir[1]RN; ni[fear]; kur[mountain(s)]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.4

A.A.5. [...] sipad a-zu-u₃ me-teš₂ ša-mu-u₃-i-i
#lem: X; sipad[shepherd]; azu[doctor]; meteš[praise]; e[bring out]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.5

@div trailer 

A.A.6. [sa]-gid₂#-da-am₃
#tr.en: @fsux{sa-gida}.
#lem: sagida[musical notation]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.6

@end trailer

@end sa-gida

@div unknown B

A.B.7. [...] X UG ba-ni-ra aga₃-kar₂ im-mi-sig₁₀
#tr.en: You defeat …….
#lem: X; X; X; rah[beat]; agakar[conquest]; sig[put into]
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.7

A.B.8. [...] sumun me ŋar im-mi-ŋa₂-ar
#tr.en: You impose silence on …….
#lem: X; sumun[old]; me[Being]; ŋar[put]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.8

A.B.9. [...] ki-bal-a-ke₄ gu₂-kiri₆ im-mi-dug₄
#tr.en: You roar a war-cry at the
#lem: X; kibala[rebel land]; gukiri[battle cry]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.9

A.B.10. [...] X kur iši su₃-ra₂-a-ba za-pa-zu im-mi#-[...]
#tr.en: rebel lands …….
#lem: X; X; kur[mountain(s)]; iš[mountain]; sud[distant]; zipaŋ[voice]; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.10

A.B.11. [... šeg₁₁] gi₄#-gi₄-a-zu-ta X
#tr.en: Your clamour …… even the distant mountains and hills.
#lem: X; šeg[voice]; gi[turn]; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.11

A.B.12. [... sug-zag]-ge₄# bi₂-gu₇# [...]
#tr.en: …… at your roaring devastate (?) …… completely.
#lem: X; sugzag[marsh edge]; gu[eat]; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.B.12

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)
